    {
      "id": "a782bee8768665a89e497586de692e6780e744f7",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1574767515,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Apologies Lars, happy to commit this.\n\nHaving said that, looking at the spec (Figure 4.15: SOME/IP header), I was surprised that the 28-bit Offset is not also included in someip_tp_flags - this would make it clearer that they are grouped together as a 4-byte (orange :)) field, and the separate offset to get wrong would not exist.\n\nBut, given that you need access to their values, my personal taste would be:\n- not to bother with a add_bitmask() here, just add add each one with with proto_tree_add_item_ret_uint()\n- you then avoid the repeated fetching and masking\n- if the mask macros are then only used in the item definitions, it might be more readable to just have them as literals in the hf definition (saves anyone reading from looking up the macro value)",
          "author": {
            "id": 6810036,
            "username": "martin.r.mathieson",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Martin Mathieson",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/030414c33f619ee28811cd9c073802ef2267d160ab2744eb8427bd49af4c7998?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/martin.r.mathieson"
          },
