    {
      "id": "d33e6138d2a85b8e1297b0d9306546f34d793705",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1576335855,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Hi Martin,\n\ndon't worry, it was caught before a release got affected. I am happy that people are using the automated build and reach out, when something looks wrong.\n\nBTW: Orange was just the best I could do in Visio back then after I had used red, green, and blue for SOME/IP-SD already. :smile: \n\nThe reason the code got that complicated is the surprising behavior of `proto_tree_add_uint` and others. I did not expect that the code would mask and shift the value passed to it, for an HF with bitmask set. :disappointed:\n\nP.S. I did some cleanup here: https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/merge_requests/12254",
          "author": {
            "id": 6878858,
            "username": "LarsVoelker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Dr. Lars Völker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
